## Appendix addition — upload session API calls

*Add to Appendix A as sections A.6 and A.7.*

### A.6 Open an upload session

**Request**

```http
POST /drives/<DRIVE-ID>/root:/Opportunities/{Opportunity Name} - {Record Id}/{filename}:/createUploadSession
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "item": {
    "@microsoft.graph.conflictBehavior": "rename"
  }
}
```

**Response**

```json
200 OK

{
  "uploadUrl": "https://bankunited.sharepoint.com/_api/v2.0/drives/<DRIVE-ID>/items/<ITEM-ID>/uploadSession?guid=<GUID>&overwrite=False&rename=True&access_token=<TOKEN>",
  "expirationDateTime": "2026-09-25T10:15:00Z"
}
```

The `uploadUrl` embeds its own authorisation and must be treated as a credential: it is
passed to the browser for the duration of the transfer and must not be logged or stored.

### A.7 Send a piece of the file

Sent by the browser, not by Apex. No `Authorization` header is attached; SharePoint
rejects the request if one is present.

**Request**

```http
PUT {uploadUrl}
Content-Range: bytes 0-5242879/47185920

<5 MB of file content>
```

**Response, intermediate pieces**

```json
202 Accepted

{
  "expirationDateTime": "2026-09-25T10:15:00Z",
  "nextExpectedRanges": ["5242880-"]
}
```

**Response, final piece**

```json
201 Created

{
  "id": "<ITEM-ID>",
  "name": "big-scan.pdf",
  "size": 47185920,
  "webUrl": "https://bankunited.sharepoint.com/sites/WB/WB%20Salesforce%20%20POC/Opportunities/...",
  "file": { "mimeType": "application/pdf" },
  "createdBy": {
    "user": { "displayName": "SharePoint App" },
    "application": { "id": "<CLIENT-ID>", "displayName": "<APP-NAME>" }
  }
}
```

`nextExpectedRanges` is what makes the transfer resumable: an interrupted upload can query
the session for the ranges still outstanding rather than starting again.
